{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":747161,\"duration_api_ms\":747313,\"num_turns\":21,\"result\":\"```json\\n{\\n  \\\"review_summary\\\": \\\"024B (scaffolder + --restore + invocation-log CI) is substantially complete against the COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE lens. D-044 is filed with all five component descriptions. ADOPT-001 §12.8 is correctly placed and carries all four required cross-references. TF-024B-002 (restore round-trip, merge-blocking) and TF-024-FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (ACC install pattern, 024C gate) are both present in STATUS.md and DISPATCH-NOTE. All ten plan-doc invariants have artefact coverage. The cascade-status self-exemption mechanism (backtick formatting in DISPATCH-NOTE) is correct by design and confirmed by test case 15b. The worked-example matrix for onboarded-operator-bump covers all stub-row edge cases (4c/d/e/f/g) per 024A R7 CRIT lesson. VERSIONING.md scope is correct: --restore flags are listed as breaking-change surfaces; no version bump is needed for purely additive flag addition. One MAJ finding blocks merge: check-invocation-log-entry.sh has no GitHub Actions workflow entry-point, meaning invariant 2's CI-enforcement requirement is aspirational, not operational. Two MIN findings are advisory. One nit is cosmetic.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh not wired into any GitHub Actions workflow — CI enforcement is non-operational\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh; .github/workflows/ (absent entry-point)\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Grep of all *.yml files in the repo returns zero matches for 'check-invocation-log-entry'. The script ships with correct implementation and full test coverage, but without a GitHub Actions workflow calling it, plan-doc invariant 2's 'CI-enforced cascade-status contract' is not satisfied operationally. No TF explicitly tracks that workflow integration will land at 024C; the current STATUS.md tracked-forward items (TF-024B-001 through TF-024B-003, TF-024-FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001) do not name a workflow-wiring deliverable.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Either (a) add a minimal .github/workflows/check-invocation-log.yml calling the script on the per-adopter DISPATCH-NOTE path as part of 024B, or (b) file a named TF (e.g. TF-024B-004) explicitly deferring workflow wiring to 024C with a clear precondition statement, and update the plan-doc §6 024B AC list to reflect that the CI step lands in 024C, not 024B.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"§12.7 Reference line D-044 addition cannot be confirmed from evidence\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.7\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The review scope stated '§12.7's Reference line gains D-044'. §12.7.3 has no standalone 'Reference:' line before §12.7.4, and no aggregate §12.7 Reference line exists between §12.7.15 and §12.8. It is possible the instruction referred to the §12.8 Reference line (which is confirmed correct), but if a distinct §12.7-level Reference line was intended, it is absent.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Confirm whether the intent was the §12.8 Reference line (already correct) or a separate §12.7-level line. If the latter, add it; if the former, clarify the review scope to avoid ambiguity in future rounds.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-CG-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Scaffolder test validates YAML syntax only — no structural schema check for canonical wrapper shape\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh line 110-117\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The AC states 'Scaffolder emits known-fixture wrapper schema-validates'. The test calls yaml.safe_load() (syntax only) and verifies substitution strings via grep. It does not validate the structural shape: permissions block, on.push trigger, jobs.policy-check-wrapper structure, or uses: reference format. A template regression (e.g. dropped permissions block) would pass the current test suite.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Add a structural schema check — either a JSON Schema file for the workflow shape validated via jsonschema/check-jsonschema, or a Python assertion block verifying the required top-level keys (on, permissions, jobs) and the uses: format pattern in the test.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"PR placeholder #<scaffolder-PR> in STATUS.md 024B chain row\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"STATUS.md 024B chain row (lines ~139-143)\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The 024B chain entry contains 'PR #<scaffolder-PR>' as a placeholder. This is expected pre-merge but should be replaced with the real PR number before the branch merges to main, otherwise the audit trail has a broken reference.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Replace #<scaffolder-PR> with the actual GitHub PR number as a merge prerequisite. Consider adding this to the pre-merge checklist in DISPATCH-NOTE or the 024B closure-doc skeleton.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\"\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"90f01e43-0f3f-4c36-b617-ed7b9b6d2f7d\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.5144423,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":13,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":169567,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":560805,\"output_tokens\":33005,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":169567,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":3,\"output_tokens\":1666,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":7381,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":23367,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":23367},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2622,\"outputTokens\":24,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002742,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":7004,\"outputTokens\":40237,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":714386,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":179418,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.5117003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"0cb35621-3906-450e-96ad-2c6db4feb84a\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
